WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.571
Started this tournament with 12
smiths from around the country.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.005
<i> We've ended with Ben's pick</i>

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:07.873
<i> from Clay Spencer
 Blacksmith Shop</i>

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.075
<i> and Dave's pick</i>

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.643
<i> from the New Agrarian School
 in Montana.</i>

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.812
Guys, you've both proven
yourselves to be worthy smiths,

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.014
and you've earned your spot

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.382
in this final round
of the competition.

00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:18.717
You guys are not only fighting
for $20,000

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:19.886
to go into your pocket,

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.222
but up to $10,000
in gear and supplies to go

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.989
back to the forge
where we met you at.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.159
In this final round,
we're sending you back home

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.893
for four days to build

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.196
a menacing blade
from history.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.565
We want you to build this...

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.868
the Moplah sword.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.170
Whoa.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.606
[Grady]<i> The Moplah sword
 traces its origins back</i>

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.142
<i> to 17th-century South India
 where it has been</i>

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.511
<i> the weapon of choice
 for the Moplah community,</i>

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.379
<i> featuring a broad,
 lightweight blade</i>

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:49.649
<i> and a concave edge that flares
 to a pronounced point,</i>

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.851
<i> making it an extremely lethal
 battle sword</i>

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.553
<i> capable of delivering
 deadly slashes</i>

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.555
<i> and destructive blows
 upon its enemies.</i>

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.290
<i> While it's distinguished by
its ornate wood or bone handle,</i>

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.559
<i> this brutal blade
 also played an important role</i>

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:03.263
<i> in the Moplah Rebellion
 of the early 20th century</i>

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.930
<i> where it was used
 to take up arms</i>

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.733
<i> against occupying
 British colonists.</i>

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.034
Gentlemen, good luck.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.204
We will see you both
in four days.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.311
[Jason]<i> I'm going to try
 to separate</i>

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:20.480
<i> my blade from Silas's blade</i>

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.182
and do San Mai Damascus.

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:26.519
So I'm going to make
two billets of Damascus.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.453
Fire in the hole.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.789
<i> I'm going to sandwich
 the two billets of Damascus</i>

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:33.326
with a piece of 80CrV.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.794
<i> I've made lots of Damascus,</i>

00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:37.496
<i> but nothing this big.</i>

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.199
<i> So, drawing it out
 and making it real wide,</i>

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:41.600
<i> that's gonna be a task.</i>

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.737
I'm at three inches.
I need another inch and a half.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:46.972
I don't know if I got enough.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:49.442
Yeah, they're makin' me earn
this 20,000.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:55.181
<i> I don't have enough meat
 to spread out,</i>

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:58.718
<i> so I gotta do the unthinkable
 and just weld up</i>

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.987
<i> a bunch of stuff on the spine</i>

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.588
to meet parameters.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.791
<i> It's about my only option
 right now.</i>

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.493
<i> And that weld is ugly,</i>

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.862
<i> but it's gonna be what
 it's gonna be at this point.</i>

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.363
<i> Yesterday, I got
 the blade quenched.</i>

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.231
[laughs]

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.133
<i> Also, I have
 all my parts made.</i>

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.701
I just gotta put it all
together.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.835
[groans]

00:02:16.935 --> 00:02:18.270
<i> This is the last step</i>

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.806
<i> in a very long
 and difficult competition.</i>

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.743
<i> I've put my entire heart
 and soul</i>

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:25.011
<i> into this whole project,</i>

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.580
and if this don't make it,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.847
then I get nothing.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.650
<i> I think, overall,
 the blade will make Ben</i>

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.687
<i> and the Clay Spencer
 Blacksmith Shop proud.</i>

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.991
[Silas]<i> The plan
 for today is to get</i>

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.760
<i> my Damascus billet
 forged out.</i>

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.796
That's the goodness right there.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.231
<i> I don't really make Damascus,</i>

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.434
and I have never made
something like this before.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:53.539
<i> Yesterday, I got my blade
 all forged out and hardened.</i>

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:54.908
Looks good.

00:02:58.343 --> 00:03:00.312
I just gave it a little flex,

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:02.381
and a crack opened right up.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.952
You can see the crack right
there in the edge of the blade.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.421
And the crack goes past

00:03:08.487 --> 00:03:11.524
where I could grind back
to meet parameters,

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:15.227
so, looks like
I'm startin' over.

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:18.363
<i> Got some 5160,
 I'm gonna forge a new blade.</i>

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:22.368
Yesterday, I got my blade
quenched and ground,

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.605
and ready to put it
all together.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.973
Okay, I think it's...
this is it.

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:29.909
I feel pretty good
about my progress.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.477
<i> I had a pretty major setback,</i>

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:34.179
<i> but I gotta rush at this point</i>

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:36.248
<i> to finish my handle.</i>

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.984
<i> Hopefully, I can bring home
 the win</i>

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.719
to Jeffrey
from the New Agrarian School.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:41.954
Hwah!

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:45.124
Bladesmiths, welcome
to our dynamic KEAL test,

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:47.994
<i> the ballistics dummy
 and sheets of ice chop.</i>

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.496
-Jason, you're up first. Ready?
-Yes, sir.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.167
[exhales]

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.238
[rock music playing]

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.389
[music fading]

00:04:19.124 --> 00:04:20.893
[suspenseful music playing]

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:25.097
[Doug] All right, Jason, let's
talk about your Moplah sword.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.667
In hitting the ice blocks,

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.802
no damage on your tip
and edge.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.171
It stayed true.

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:35.374
In chopping
into the ballistics dummy,

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:38.110
very deep, deep cuts.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.679
And overall, your weapon,

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:41.781
it'll KEAL.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.449
Thank you, sir.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.918
-All right, Silas. You ready?
-Yes, sir.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:52.025
[hard rock music playing]

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:07.774
[ice block clattering]

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.080
[music stops]

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.217
Good job. [chuckling]

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:20.919
[suspenseful music playing]

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:25.558
[Doug] All right, Silas, let's
talk about your Moplah sword.

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:26.426
First up,

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:29.528
this thing is light.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.330
I could use velocity

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.499
to cut cleanly
on the ice blocks,

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.467
and those are one
of the deepest cuts

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.137
we have on a ballistics dummy,
but in the test,

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.739
you have two spots here

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.640
where I can get
my fingernail into that,

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:46.145
but that's because you have
a very, very acute

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.780
and sharp edge here,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.615
and it will KEAL.

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:53.553
[dramatic music playing]

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:59.125
[chuckling]

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:02.328
All right, gentlemen, welcome
to our dynamic strength test,

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:05.564
the chain mail and skull chop.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.066
Jason, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.200
-Yes, sir.
-Okay.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.970
[dramatic music playing]

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.944
[whacking]

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.846
[whacking and clattering]

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.648
[rock music playing]

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.918
[grunting]

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.056
[grunting and clattering]

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.926
[grunting]

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:38.531
-[grunting]
-[music stops]

00:06:40.432 --> 00:06:43.403
[tense music playing]

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:47.106
All right, Jason.
This thing's a beast.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.375
Everything's still right
and tight.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:50.642
I really like what you did here.

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:52.878
This is really
just beautiful work.

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:55.647
It's a great-looking weapon,
it did the job, and it held up.

00:06:55.714 --> 00:06:58.016
-So, nicely done.
-Thank you.

00:06:58.116 --> 00:07:00.252
Silas, you ready?

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:01.721
Let's do this.

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:02.921
I'm going to.

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:04.990
[laughter]

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:07.960
[tense music playing]

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.099
[exhales]

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.703
[grunting and whacking]

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.443
[rock music playing]

00:07:27.813 --> 00:07:29.816
[grunting]

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:38.724
[grunting]

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.860
Good job.

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:43.996
[suspenseful music playing]

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.665
[Dave] All right, Silas,
your handle,

00:07:46.765 --> 00:07:49.768
issue I have with it
is that the handle is rounded

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:53.339
in a way that it wants
to turn in my hand

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:54.807
when I impact things.

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:58.311
I couldn't maintain a grip.

00:07:58.411 --> 00:07:59.978
That's a big issue.

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.179
Thank you.

00:08:01.513 --> 00:08:03.816
[dramatic music playing]

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:10.622
Gentlemen, it's been
a wild ride, guys.

00:08:10.722 --> 00:08:12.992
I've been honored to travel
across America with these guys,

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.428
visiting all four
of the forges we went to,

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.196
watching you two work
the entire time

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:18.363
through this competition.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.766
I can guarantee
that both Jeffrey and Belz

00:08:20.832 --> 00:08:22.735
would be extremely proud
of your work.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.870
But unfortunately, only one
of you guys can take home

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:28.207
the $20,000 for yourself,
the $10,000 to go back

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:29.508
into the forge
you're representing,

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.443
and the title
of<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.713
The judges did make a decision,

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.814
and today's
<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:38.450
and the winner of
the On the Road tournament is...

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:41.353
[music intensifying]

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.556
Jason. Very well done.

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:46.025
Now, Silas, you crushed it
throughout the competition,

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:48.227
but unfortunately, your time
in this tournament has ended.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:50.929
I'm gonna have to ask you
to step off the Forge floor.

00:08:51.429 --> 00:08:53.198
[Silas]<i> I feel disappointed.</i>

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:56.468
<i> I certainly made some mistakes
 during my home forge,</i>

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.837
and in a close competition,

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:00.406
mistakes are what matter,

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:01.974
<i> but I'm still really proud</i>

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:04.677
<i> of representing
 the New Agrarian School.</i>

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:07.245
I wish that I had been able
to bring it home for them,

00:09:07.345 --> 00:09:09.749
<i> but that's competition.</i>

00:09:10.782 --> 00:09:12.484
[Grady] Jason, congratulations.

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:14.153
You are now
a<i> Forged in Fire</i> champion.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.521
You came out on top
of this On the Road tournament,

00:09:16.588 --> 00:09:18.691
and you're getting a check
not only for $20,000

00:09:18.757 --> 00:09:21.960
going in your pocket,
but you're bringing back $10,000

00:09:22.027 --> 00:09:23.929
for gear and supplies
to go back to Belz

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:25.764
and the Clay Spencer
Blacksmith Shop.

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:27.767
-Very, very well done.
-[applause]

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:29.902
[Jason]
<i> I'm a</i> Forged in Fire<i> champion,</i>

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:32.404
and I'm in shock
and awe disbelief.

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:35.507
<i> It's been an honor
and a privilege to go this far,</i>

00:09:35.574 --> 00:09:37.876
<i> to be the winner,
 and to be bringing</i>

00:09:37.943 --> 00:09:40.378
<i> $10,000 in equipment
 and gear for John C. Campbell,</i>

00:09:40.445 --> 00:09:41.947
<i> and my wife will be happy.</i>

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.982
I'm comin' home
with 20 grand, hon.

00:09:44.082 --> 00:09:45.017
[laughs]

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:46.852
[rock music playing]

